{
 "about": "Real services per trade (SVC appointment and crew model). `share` = relative customers, `rel` = relative price (both normalised on install so share x rel adds up to 1 and the company's going ticket is unchanged), `min` = chair, bay, car or crew time of one job in minutes, `cons` = consumables as a share of the price, `dir` = other direct cost as a share of the price (lab fee, car running, implant part). Costs are scaled on install so the weighted cost of the whole menu equals the trade's cost-of-sales share in trades.json (the books never move). `m`: svc, sub (recurring: `visits` jobs per `period` weeks, `churn` per period) or stk (retail stock bought at `cons` of the price, `lead` days). `pack` = jobs sold together. `extra` entries are the add-item catalogue of the trade. Units are the trade's own unit (lesson, treatment, car, cleaning hour); a pack or block is priced per unit. `fteHours` = hours one full-time person works a week. `skillLabel` and `resLabel` on an item override the trade's when the job needs another person or room.",
